def rank_components(clean, corrupt, patched, threshold):
    if clean == corrupt:
        raise ValueError('clean and corrupted runs give the same metric')
    fracs = [(i, (p - corrupt) / (clean - corrupt)) for i, p in enumerate(patched)]
    kept = [(i, f) for i, f in fracs if f >= threshold - 1e-12]
    return sorted(kept, key=lambda t: -t[1])
```

Component 2's patch makes things slightly *worse* (fraction below zero) — this happens in real models too, where some components push against the behaviour. Fractions above 1 also occur when a patch overshoots. Neither is a bug in the metric; both are information about the circuit. Remember that single-component patches miss behaviours that need several components at once, which is why path patching and automated circuit discovery exist.

